  "comment": "No source is published. Each channel's CV jack multiplies its level knob rather than adding to it, at a tenth per volt, so a cable resting at 0V silences that channel and the knob does nothing while it is in. A channel's own output jack carries the mono sum of its left and right inputs, not a stereo pair, and patching it clears that channel from both main accumulators. The Stereo Split switch is only consulted for the L(M) jack: a channel patched on R alone reaches the right output only, whichever way the switch is set. One light is configured and follows the switch, but it has no position in the census and cannot be clicked."
